## psc/sema/check/lint.pengu — lints opcionales del checker.
##
## De momento hay uno solo: `W0008`, detrás de `--lint=cow`.
##
## La heurística marca copiar un contenedor y mutar la copia dentro de un
## bucle. El programa sigue siendo correcto (COW lo hace seguro), pero paga
## una clonación del búfer por vuelta: mover la copia fuera del bucle, o
## limpiar y rellenar el mismo contenedor, evita el coste.
##
## El lint es **opt-in** a propósito: sin el flag, ningún proyecto ve avisos
## nuevos.

insignia sema_lint_

import psc.ast.kind as pskind
import psc.ast.node as psast
import psc.sema.ast as astutil
import psc.sema.diagnostics as sdiag
import psc.sema.state as state

## `true` si el nombre de método muta el contenedor.
##
## `push`/`append` y `put`/`insert` añaden, `remove`/`clear` quitan; en los
## cuatro casos el receptor necesita un búfer exclusivo.
##
## ## Memoria
## Compara literales; no asigna.
weave is_mutating_method with name as string into bool:
    if name == "push" or name == "append" or name == "put" or name == "insert":
        return true
    if name == "remove" or name == "clear" or name == "pop":
        return true
    return false

## Recorre el cuerpo buscando bucles y aplica la heurística a cada uno.
##
## ## Memoria
## O(profundidad del AST); no retiene nodos.
weave lint_cow_loops with s as ref to state.SemaState, body as int into void:
    if body < 0:
        return
    calling walk_loops with s, body

## Desciende el AST y llama a `lint_loop` en cada bucle.
##
## ## Memoria
## Recursión acotada por la profundidad del AST.
weave walk_loops with s as ref to state.SemaState, node as int into void:
    if node < 0:
        return
    var ast as ref to psast.PsAst is s->ast
    var k as pskind.NodeKind is calling astutil.kind_of with ast, node
    if k == pskind.NodeKind.NdWhileStmt or k == pskind.NodeKind.NdForRangeStmt or k == pskind.NodeKind.NdForInStmt:
        calling lint_loop with s, node
    var n as int is calling astutil.child_count with ast, node
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        var ch as int is calling astutil.node_child with ast, node, i
        if ch >= 0:
            calling walk_loops with s, ch
        set i is i + 1

## Texto del token `slot` de un nodo, o `""`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve owned; el llamador lo libera.
weave child_text with s as ref to state.SemaState, node as int, slot as int into string:
    var ast as ref to psast.PsAst is s->ast
    var tk as int is calling astutil.token_child with ast, node, slot
    if tk < 0:
        return ""
    return calling astutil.token_text with s->src, s->lex, tk

## `true` si el nodo de tipo nombra `list`, `map` o `string`.
##
## Se mira la forma sintáctica (no el tipo resuelto) para que el lint funcione
## también en tipos genéricos aún sin instanciar.
##
## ## Memoria
## Libera el texto que pide; no retiene nada.
weave type_node_is_cow with s as ref to state.SemaState, tnode as int into bool:
    if tnode < 0:
        return false
    var ast as ref to psast.PsAst is s->ast
    var k as pskind.NodeKind is calling astutil.kind_of with ast, tnode
    if k == pskind.NodeKind.NdListType or k == pskind.NodeKind.NdMapType:
        return true
    if k == pskind.NodeKind.NdBaseType or k == pskind.NodeKind.NdVarRef:
        var txt as string is calling child_text with s, tnode, 0
        var hit as bool is txt == "string"
        banish txt
        return hit
    return false

## Acumula copias (`var x is y`) y receptores mutados del subárbol.
##
## ## Memoria
## Empuja en las listas del llamador; no libera nada.
weave scan_loop with s as ref to state.SemaState, node as int, decls as ref to vector of int, muts as ref to vector of string into void:
    if node < 0:
        return
    var ast as ref to psast.PsAst is s->ast
    var k as pskind.NodeKind is calling astutil.kind_of with ast, node
    if k == pskind.NodeKind.NdVarDecl:
        var tn as int is calling astutil.node_child with ast, node, 1
        var vn as int is calling astutil.node_child with ast, node, 2
        if tn >= 0 and vn >= 0:
            if (calling astutil.kind_of with ast, vn) == pskind.NodeKind.NdVarRef:
                if calling type_node_is_cow with s, tn:
                    calling decls.push with node
    else if k == pskind.NodeKind.NdCallingExpr:
        var tg as int is calling astutil.node_child with ast, node, 0
        if tg >= 0:
            var step as int is calling astutil.node_child with ast, tg, 1
            if step >= 0:
                var mname as string is calling child_text with s, step, 0
                var recv as string is calling child_text with s, tg, 0
                if (calling is_mutating_method with mname) and (recv length) > 0:
                    calling muts.push with recv
                else:
                    banish recv
                banish mname
    var n as int is calling astutil.child_count with ast, node
    var i as int is 0
    while i < n:
        var ch as int is calling astutil.node_child with ast, node, i
        if ch >= 0:
            calling scan_loop with s, ch, decls, muts
        set i is i + 1

## Aplica la heurística a un bucle concreto.
##
## ## Memoria
## Listas locales liberadas con `banish`.
weave lint_loop with s as ref to state.SemaState, loop as int into void:
    var decls as vector of int is vector of int
    defer banish decls
    var muts as vector of string is vector of string
    defer banish muts
    calling scan_loop with s, loop, (sigil of decls), (sigil of muts)
    var ast as ref to psast.PsAst is s->ast
    var i as int is 0
    while i < decls.len:
        var dn as int is decls at i
        var name as string is calling child_text with s, dn, 0
        var onode as int is calling astutil.node_child with ast, dn, 2
        var origin as string is calling child_text with s, onode, 0
        var hit as bool is false
        var j as int is 0
        while j < muts.len:
            if (muts at j) == name:
                set hit is true
            set j is j + 1
        if hit:
            var st as int is calling astutil.start_of with ast, dn
            var en as int is calling astutil.end_of with ast, dn
            var msg as string is "copy '{name}' is mutated inside a loop: every iteration clones the buffer"
            var help as string is "Move the copy out of the loop, or clear and refill it instead of copying '{origin}'."
            calling sdiag.node_info with s->bag, s->src, sdiag.WARN_COW_LOOP, st, en, msg, help
            banish msg
            banish help
        banish name
        banish origin
        set i is i + 1
